1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,300
Okame Special is brought to you
by Bandai Namco Entertainment and

2
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:08,680
our sponsors.

3
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,680
This is Kameari.

4
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:34,880
Right.

5
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,900
Let's send the out-of-office number.

6
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:44,000
You can go home now.

7
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:47,580
What's with that hand?

8
00:00:57,760 --> 00:00:58,820
What's his problem?

9
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,840
Good morning, senior.

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,700
It's Nakagawa and Reiko.

11
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:13,420
What are you doing this early?
Writing a reprimand report?

12
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:14,880
This is it.

13
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:15,860
Propellers?

14
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:17,940
Yeah, for the drone.

15
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:20,420
You're making a drone by hand?

16
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:21,680
What choice did I have?

17
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:24,080
I was going to buy one with my summer bonus,

18
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:27,200
but the debt collectors took every last yen.

19
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:28,320
Damn it!

20
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:28,800
What are you doing?

21
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:02,980
Eeeeeh!

22
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:11,800
I had it, you see.
I was born in America, France, so...

23
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:13,740
What?

24
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:15,060
What?

25
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:19,280
Ryo-san, you're being naive!

26
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:22,300
Did you really think a simple
disguise would let you escape us?

27
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:24,946
Now then, the debts that have piled up,

28
00:02:24,996 --> 00:02:26,980
you'll be paying every
last yen of them, right?

29
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:29,740
Fine, I'll pay. Just wait.

30
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:32,780
You're the one being naive!

31
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:41,840
It's going exactly as planned.

32
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:53,300
Trying to take my summer bonus?
That's a million years too early!

33
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:56,400
Which one?

34
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,560
Higurashi

35
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:06,000
You, who only wake up in an Olympic year,
once every four years,

36
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,980
So this year's the Olympics?

37
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:09,900
Once every four years.

38
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:13,300
I've been sleeping for eight years,
you know.

39
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:16,820
Now that you mention it,
it's been ages since we last met.

40
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:17,760
Shut up.

41
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:22,500
Because you didn't wake me four years ago,
Homes changed its members.

42
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:26,340
I hear AKB48 is the big thing right now.

43
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:29,100
For someone who was asleep,
you sure know a lot.

44
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:30,660
Shut up, shut up.

45
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:39,380
While I was asleep, they formed SKE,
NMB, HKT, NGT, and even Nogizaka46!

46
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:43,660
Why does only Nogizaka get the "46"?

47
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:45,340
How would I know about that?

48
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:47,340
Be quiet!

49
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:19,400
I'm going to be getting it into production and sales,
you see.

50
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:22,460
I've got a prototype right here with me.

51
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:24,620
I'll bring it in next time.

52
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:28,820
After all, what you really need to have

53
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:30,360
is celebrity friends, that's what!

54
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:32,380
Senpai, please stop!

55
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:34,840
Chief!

56
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:37,580
Don't get the wrong idea, Chief!

57
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:39,000
What are you fooling around for?

58
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,240
Anyway, let's just forgive him.

59
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:42,560
I'm heading out on patrol.

60
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:44,260
Hey, you! Ryotsu!

61
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:48,940
That man is absolutely hopeless.

62
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:18,400
Should I take it, I wonder

63
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:22,200
If I stay a kid like this

64
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:24,500
we get laughed at

65
00:05:25,170 --> 00:05:29,580
even if I stir up some energy somewhere

66
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:31,320
Pachinko, there's a reason for it

67
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:34,660
A yawn, and nothing changes

68
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:38,560
The streets feel strangely gentle

69
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:46,600
From the pointed-hat water tower

70
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:52,820
The sun sinks toward the vast sky

71
00:05:56,300 --> 00:06:01,280
Tomorrow, too, it ends just like this

72
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:06,520
Katsushika, Shibamata, happiness lost again

73
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:09,900
Because I'm the fool who only realized it

74
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:20,880
The last day

75
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:36,940
The password is... mountain.

76
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,040
River.

77
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:39,020
Okay.

78
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:47,440
Wasn't this place shut down half a year ago?

79
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:51,500
What's that high-tech-looking antenna?

80
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,300
It's super suspicious.

81
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:58,060
The password is... mountain.

82
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:58,940
River.

83
00:07:58,940 --> 00:07:59,760
Okay.

84
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:15,440
Kanpē!

85
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:18,360
Kankichi, how did you find this place?

86
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:21,640
It looked so shady that
I came over in a panic.

87
00:08:22,060 --> 00:08:24,860
Anyway,
what is this high-tech-looking facility?

88
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:27,720
Surprised

89
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:32,140
We've been totally hooked on an
American forensic crime drama lately.

90
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:34,580
We recreated it to look
just like the real thing.

91
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:36,700
So it's just playing pretend?

92
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:39,420
Playing pretend? You're naive, Kankichi.

93
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:43,920
We've even succeeded in hacking the
Metropolitan Police's main computer.

94
00:08:44,660 --> 00:08:45,380
No way!

95
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:46,460
Heh heh heh.

96
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:47,960
Agent Tomiyoshi

97
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:52,220
From the footage of the security cameras the
Metropolitan Police installed around Tokyo,

98
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:54,560
find the origin of this transmission for us.

99
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,340
Roger.

100
00:09:04,980 --> 00:09:06,400
Don't be shocked just yet.

101
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:10,240
Even the secret files on every
Metropolitan Police officer,

102
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:11,780
No way, it's the real deal!

103
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:14,220
Your wicked deeds, too,

104
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,080
the Eiffel Tower,

105
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,540
skyscrapers,

106
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:21,060
you've blown up TV stations more than once,
haven't you?

107
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:24,740
The Metropolitan Police really leave
some outrageous data lying around.

108
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:28,500
The reason? You two are totally
committing unauthorized access!

109
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:30,100
Everyone's under arrest.

110
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:32,220
Don't be so stiff about it.

111
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:34,860
You can rewrite data easily, too.

112
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:36,100
Really?

113
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,820
Mio-san, what's this?
Should I erase it for you?

114
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:40,080
Yeah, please do.

115
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:43,640
Keep the Secret Knight stuff quiet, okay?

116
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:45,660
Only if you give me a discount.

117
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:52,340
And now, finally,

118
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:55,800
I'm officially a good police officer,
after all.

119
00:09:57,180 --> 00:10:00,080
You lot, don't you dare use it for crime!

120
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:02,760
It's about time for my part-time job.

121
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:04,080
See you.

122
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:07,300
Princess Sabrina

123
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:09,980
is planning to kidnap her for ransom money.

124
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,440
With the pride of the
Japanese police at stake,

125
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:19,920
we absolutely cannot allow such a thing.

126
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:23,240
Princess Sabrina is known
as a true Japanophile,

127
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:28,660
and she reportedly wants to tour the old downtown
where the Edo Castle ruins remain during her visit.

128
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:30,120
Ah

129
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:36,040
So that means they might also
come to our Katsushika area?

130
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:38,700
Is there a possibility they'll be visiting?

131
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,260
Is that quite conceivable?

132
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:43,980
Anyway,

133
00:10:44,030 --> 00:10:48,080
keep in close contact with the
princess's aides and handle security.

134
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:53,880
Kankichi, are you out on a delivery?

135
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:56,600
Yeah, Raymond, I'm just going out for a bit.

136
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:08,900
It should be somewhere around here,
the Jansō...

137
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:12,160
A traffic accident?

138
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:16,300
Hey, hey, what's going on? What's going on?

139
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:26,440
This is non-electronic language.

140
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:30,080
Help!

141
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:32,720
You're gonna say it?!

142
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:36,840
Hey, you!

143
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:13,280
Aaaaaah!

144
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:14,960
Eeeeeeh!

145
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:17,080
Eeeeeeh!

146
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,000
Eeeeeeh!

147
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,260
Eeeeeeh!

148
00:12:20,260 --> 00:12:21,560
Eeeeeeh!

149
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:22,400
Eeeeeeh!

150
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:22,440
Eeeeeeh!

151
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:23,260
Eeeeeeh!

152
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:26,040
What a persistent pest.

153
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:27,660
This'll make us late!

154
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,180
Damn it!

155
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:45,260
Right!

156
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:47,100
Let's ask those guys for backup.

157
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:49,120
Kanbē!

158
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:51,780
A kidnapping just happened
at the Kanda intersection.

159
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:56,360
I found the van!

160
00:12:56,820 --> 00:12:59,060
I'll guide you,
so follow my instructions, okay?

161
00:12:59,060 --> 00:13:00,140
Roger!

162
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,540
They just turned onto the
street with Super Kanga Sushi!

163
00:13:03,540 --> 00:13:05,360
Alright, we'll cut them off!

164
00:13:20,140 --> 00:13:21,260
It's that guy again!

165
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:22,060
Hiromono!

166
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:22,740
Grab him!

167
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:23,460
Yes!

168
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:27,140
Eeeeeeeh

169
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:30,920
Aaaaaaah

170
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,080
Aaaaaaah

171
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:33,560
Aaaaaaah

172
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:40,240
Hey, pull yourself together!

173
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:41,020
Damn it

174
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:45,140
Don't come any closer

175
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:46,320
I'll kill you

176
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:47,840
Pulling a dirty trick

177
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:50,080
Put your hands up and step aside

178
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:50,900
Got it

179
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:53,060
This is a make-or-break moment

180
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:55,660
What the hell is this!

181
00:13:58,520 --> 00:13:59,360
Ma-

182
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:01,060
Damn it! Ah-!

183
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:01,420
Ngh!

184
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:04,840
Daaaah!

185
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:08,660
Excelator!

186
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,040
Leader?

187
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:18,440
Damn it!

188
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:23,725
Well done, Kankichi.

189
00:14:23,775 --> 00:14:26,460
I'll report it to the police myself.

190
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:27,600
Understood.

191
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:30,200
Thank you for saving us.

192
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:32,200
You're safe now.

193
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:37,700
L-lemon!

194
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:46,740
Well, that's good, that's good.

195
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:54,020
This is no laughing matter! One wrong step and both
the princess and I would have gone to the afterlife!

196
00:14:54,600 --> 00:15:01,960
Still, saving the princess deserves a commendation from the Police Commissioner.
Though I can't make deliveries anymore because of it.

197
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:07,460
Then, as an apology, I already delivered some top-grade sushi.
That's good to hear.

198
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:10,680
I'll deduct the big money
from Kawakichi's part-time pay.

199
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:11,480
No, buhehe!

200
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:13,840
You're a demon!

201
00:15:16,140 --> 00:15:17,740
But they really do look alike, don't they.

202
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:19,320
The princess and Lemon.

203
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:23,440
When I first saw Lemon-san too,

204
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:25,920
I thought I was looking at
my own reflection in a mirror.

205
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:27,840
Lemon thought the same thing.

206
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:30,140
Apart from the hairstyle, they're identical.

207
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:34,040
Well, don't you speak like
a period drama character?

208
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:37,040
Does the princess understand period dramas?

209
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:39,580
Yes, please call me Sabrina.

210
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:41,680
I heard it on the news.

211
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:45,220
Apparently she mastered Japanese
through dramas and movies.

212
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:47,080
That's quite impressive.

213
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:49,780
Sabrina, if you like period dramas,

214
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:51,900
there are DVDs in Lemon's room.

215
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:53,260
Shall we watch them together?

216
00:15:53,260 --> 00:15:54,020
Yes.

217
00:15:57,220 --> 00:16:00,180
May I bring some sushi along?

218
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:01,340
Sure.

219
00:16:02,980 --> 00:16:03,820
This way.

220
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:08,920
You even like sushi?
I like you more and more.

221
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:14,340
That's so cool!

222
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:18,620
Lemon, what's that spear-like
thing the princess is using?

223
00:16:18,620 --> 00:16:19,980
It's a naginata.

224
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,360
A naginata.

225
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:24,480
That's right, we have one at home too!

226
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,560
Great!

227
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:27,180
I'd really love to see it.

228
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:29,360
They won't let us use the real one, though.

229
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,580
But we can use a practice one.

230
00:16:31,580 --> 00:16:33,380
This is how you hold it.

231
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:34,060
Yes.

232
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:35,040
...and

233
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,020
...and

234
00:16:36,540 --> 00:16:36,780
...and

235
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:47,080
We're not customers.

236
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:51,380
We heard Princess Sabrina was here,
so we went to pick her up.

237
00:16:51,740 --> 00:16:53,560
How did you find this place?

238
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:55,560
I told them.

239
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:59,060
Your grandpa contacted me.

240
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:02,100
I hear you protected the
princess from the kidnappers.

241
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:03,340
Heh, well...

242
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:07,020
That's when the princess's aides

243
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:08,245
asked about you during her stay in Japan,

244
00:17:08,295 --> 00:17:11,940
requesting that you guard the princess.

245
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:15,280
It's a great honor.
You'll accept, won't you?

246
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:21,040
No way! They fired automatic rifles at us!
I'm turning this down!

247
00:17:21,300 --> 00:17:24,180
Headquarters says they'll give us a special bonus,
too, but

248
00:17:28,540 --> 00:17:30,060
A special bonus?

249
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:30,480
Sooo?

250
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:33,480
Bo-nus, bo-nus, bo-nus!

251
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:34,320
Woohoo!

252
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:35,040
Right?

253
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,200
You'll take the job, won't you!

254
00:17:37,340 --> 00:17:38,480
Leave it to me!

255
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:41,640
For the princess,
I'd go through fire and water!

256
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:47,460
Each of you gets your own room.

257
00:17:47,460 --> 00:17:52,800
For a first timer, you're doing quite well.

258
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:55,340
Thank you very much.

259
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:02,780
Sabrina!
Your aides have come to pick you up!

260
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:07,180
I want to stay here a little longer.

261
00:18:07,780 --> 00:18:08,780
Sabrina...

262
00:18:08,780 --> 00:18:11,180
Kankichi! Lemon, please ask him too!

263
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:13,320
Sabrina's schedule is packed solid,

264
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:16,040
so apparently she can't
go anywhere she likes.

265
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:17,920
Well, even if you say that...

266
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:27,340
I've got a good idea!

267
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:30,200
Sabrina and Lemon look so alike.

268
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:32,560
How about they swap places for just one day?

269
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:34,680
That's a good idea!

270
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,000
Don't be ridiculous!

271
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:40,040
If we did that,
Lemon might get kidnapped, you know!

272
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:42,060
I'll never allow it.

273
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:43,660
Please!

274
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:44,740
Absolutely not!

275
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:49,220
If you allow them to swap,
I'll give you this.

276
00:18:49,220 --> 00:18:51,440
Like I'd want a pendant or anything.

277
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:54,192
Kankichi, take a good look.

278
00:18:54,242 --> 00:18:56,600
It's a sparkling diamond.

279
00:18:57,580 --> 00:18:58,860
D-diamond?

280
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:03,560
Kree, kree.

281
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:05,540
Please, take this.

282
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:07,960
No, no way.

283
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:16,020
Little boy, I think I'll pretend
I never heard about the swap.

284
00:19:50,340 --> 00:19:52,080
This Kochikame Special so far

285
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,560
is brought to you by
Bandai Namco Entertainment

286
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:58,860
and the sponsors you see.

287
00:20:01,740 --> 00:20:02,640
It's a debriefing.

288
00:20:03,460 --> 00:20:06,140
What was the reason the
kidnapping failed this time?

289
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:07,880
Yes.

290
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:11,260
I think it's because the leader got
punched after accepting the sushi.

291
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:12,460
Shut up.

292
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:16,060
The leader's mistakes are your mistakes,
as his subordinates!

293
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,340
Understand?

294
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:21,660
Yes! The kidnapping's
failure was our mistake!

295
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:24,760
That's right!
Don't make any mistakes tomorrow!

296
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:25,980
Y-yes, sir! Yes!

297
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:35,100
Honestly,
Senpai is quite a handful, isn't he?

298
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:38,900
But he is trying to grant Princess Sabrina's wish,
after all.

299
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:40,040
That's just like Ryo-chan.

300
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:43,520
What's got you in such a hurry?

301
00:20:43,940 --> 00:20:48,380
That idiot was asked to guard Princess
Sabrina and then just ditched it.

302
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:50,460
If it were Ryo-chan, he would surely

303
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:51,460
Reiko-san.

304
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,460
Is something the matter?

305
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:55,920
It's nothing.

306
00:20:55,920 --> 00:21:00,000
Leave the princess's
guard to me and Kei-chan.

307
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,160
Right then, Sabrina.

308
00:21:02,680 --> 00:21:05,560
Today I'll show you around Shitamachi.

309
00:21:06,280 --> 00:21:06,640
Yes.

310
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:15,680
Ryo-chan.

311
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:17,660
Granny, you're still alive?

312
00:21:17,660 --> 00:21:20,180
What are you talking about?
Here, rice crackers.

313
00:21:20,180 --> 00:21:24,020
Thanks. Here you go, Japanese rice crackers.

314
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:25,020
Thank you.

315
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:27,360
Delicious.

316
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:30,040
Right? Well, see you.

317
00:21:30,620 --> 00:21:32,340
Ryo-chan, want some ningyo-yaki?

318
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:34,120
Another time.

319
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:37,000
Ryo-chan, sell us your apps.

320
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,560
Another time.

321
00:21:39,060 --> 00:21:40,300
You're popular.

322
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:41,480
Yeah, right now.

323
00:21:41,480 --> 00:21:43,700
Ryo-san, pay back your debt.

324
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:44,460
Shut up.

325
00:21:55,220 --> 00:21:56,700
Shitamachi is the best!

326
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:58,620
I'm glad to hear that.

327
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:05,800
Sabrina, what do you want for lunch?

328
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:06,820
Monja!

329
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:09,580
Typical of someone who loves Shitamachi.

330
00:22:10,860 --> 00:22:13,500
Look, that's the Skytree.

331
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:15,200
Wow, it's so tall!

332
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:16,980
How tall is it?

333
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:19,220
It's 634 meters.

334
00:22:19,220 --> 00:22:22,600
As a free-standing broadcasting tower,
it's the tallest in the world.

335
00:22:22,600 --> 00:22:23,180
Amazing!

336
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,360
Just as expected of a first-class hotel.

337
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:45,240
made with carefully sieved
domestic ingredients,

338
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:48,000
and subtly topped with French truffles.

339
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:49,940
So how does it taste?

340
00:22:52,680 --> 00:22:55,380
Reiko, Nakagawa, don't drink that!

341
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,520
Nakagawa, wake up!

342
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:03,980
There was sleeping medicine in it!

343
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:05,400
Lemon-chan!

344
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:07,260
Contact Kankichi!

345
00:23:09,260 --> 00:23:10,300
Let go!

346
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:21,700
Delicious!

347
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:23,500
Monja is the best!

348
00:23:23,700 --> 00:23:24,440
I see!

349
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:25,380
Hehehe.

350
00:23:25,380 --> 00:23:29,380
Monja is a representative B-grade gourmet of Shitamachi,
after all.

351
00:23:32,260 --> 00:23:33,040
Nakagawa

352
00:23:33,570 --> 00:23:34,900
What's wrong, Nakagawa!

353
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:38,740
L-Lemon-chan has been kidnapped...

354
00:23:39,660 --> 00:23:41,420
Nakagawa! Hey! Nakagawa!

355
00:23:42,780 --> 00:23:44,040
What? Lemon?

356
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:48,180
There should be a car that left
the Grand Hotel within five minutes!

357
00:23:48,340 --> 00:23:49,700
Look into it right away!

358
00:23:49,980 --> 00:23:50,640
Got it.

359
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:54,020
If anything happens to Lemon...

360
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:57,620
Don't worry, Sabrina!
Lemon is a smart and strong girl!

361
00:23:57,880 --> 00:24:00,180
Besides, I'll definitely rescue her!

362
00:24:01,460 --> 00:24:06,940
Apart from taxis and hired cars, the only vehicles I see are
laundry service vans carrying sheets out the back entrance.

363
00:24:06,940 --> 00:24:08,560
Yeah, that's suspicious.

364
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:09,440
Bingo.

365
00:24:09,440 --> 00:24:13,620
The car was the same stolen one from yesterday,
just repainted.

366
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:17,020
Use the security camera
footage to track that car.

367
00:24:18,280 --> 00:24:21,260
Hang in there, Lemon, until I get there.

368
00:24:24,800 --> 00:24:25,520
Understood.

369
00:24:26,020 --> 00:24:27,820
I want to confirm the princess's safety.

370
00:24:27,820 --> 00:24:28,560
Let me hear their voice...

371
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:31,620
Hey, hey, hello? Hello?

372
00:24:34,260 --> 00:24:35,240
Did you trace the call...?

373
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:39,680
So, what did the kidnappers say?

374
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:45,300
They demanded 10 billion yen in cash.

375
00:24:47,060 --> 00:24:48,340
10 billion yen?

376
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:53,680
Chief, there's a call from a
man who says he's Kankichi Ryotsu.

377
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:55,480
Ryotsu, you say?

378
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:57,560
Y-yes, he's my subordinate.

379
00:24:59,420 --> 00:25:00,980
Switch to the monitor.

380
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:05,800
We've identified the car the kidnappers used,
so I'm sending the footage to you.

381
00:25:08,460 --> 00:25:10,100
How did you figure it out?

382
00:25:10,700 --> 00:25:15,920
I checked the security camera footage around the hotel
right after the kidnapping happened.

383
00:25:16,320 --> 00:25:16,940
How come?

384
00:25:16,940 --> 00:25:19,660
How are you able to do something like that?

385
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:21,960
And where exactly are you right now?

386
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:24,420
That doesn't matter.

387
00:25:24,420 --> 00:25:27,060
Anyway,
find the kidnappers' car as fast as you can.

388
00:25:27,060 --> 00:25:29,860
Once you know, contact my cell phone.

389
00:25:29,860 --> 00:25:30,520
Well then.

390
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:34,440
Ri-atsu, ri-atsu!

391
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:36,480
Agent Kanbe.

392
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:40,240
I found it before Sakura Dom,
who's been lagging behind!

393
00:25:41,940 --> 00:25:42,860
It's Asakusabashi.

394
00:25:42,860 --> 00:25:43,820
Well done!

395
00:25:43,820 --> 00:25:45,400
Keep tailing them.

396
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:48,700
Kankichi, take this with you.

397
00:25:49,480 --> 00:25:50,440
That's a big help.

398
00:25:51,840 --> 00:25:53,080
Lemon-chan is...

399
00:25:53,700 --> 00:25:55,900
Yes, yes, roger that.

400
00:25:57,860 --> 00:26:00,440
Sorry, but today's training is cancelled.

401
00:26:01,020 --> 00:26:05,040
Oof, here we go.

402
00:26:06,940 --> 00:26:07,760
Ryusenodana!

403
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:09,520
Oraa!

404
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:11,980
Wow! That's so cool!

405
00:26:15,540 --> 00:26:17,060
Oryoryoryoryoryoryo!

406
00:26:18,940 --> 00:26:19,700
Shah!

407
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:22,700
You got here fast!

408
00:26:22,980 --> 00:26:25,320
I came speeding over here at 200 km/h,
you know.

409
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:26,260
Alright!

410
00:26:27,420 --> 00:26:27,820
Guts!

411
00:26:30,460 --> 00:26:31,620
I'm going too.

412
00:26:31,620 --> 00:26:34,020
No! It's too dangerous!

413
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:34,980
But...

414
00:26:38,340 --> 00:26:39,440
I want to go too.

415
00:26:40,180 --> 00:26:41,240
Damn it.

416
00:26:45,660 --> 00:26:50,720
Ryo-chan, I'm sorry. We were right there with her,
and Lemon-chan got kidnapped.

417
00:26:51,520 --> 00:26:54,660
It can't be helped.
Those guys were just better than us.

418
00:26:55,120 --> 00:26:58,780
More importantly, you showed up at the right time.
Please look after Sabrina.

419
00:26:59,100 --> 00:27:01,680
For everything else,
follow Kankichi's instructions inside.

420
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:08,560
Sorry! Wait for me.
I'll definitely bring Lemon back.

421
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:08,780
Really?

422
00:27:09,820 --> 00:27:10,440
Really.

423
00:27:10,440 --> 00:27:11,740
Promise?

424
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:13,060
Promise.

425
00:27:13,060 --> 00:27:15,400
Okay. You'd better keep that promise.

426
00:27:16,260 --> 00:27:17,240
Absolutely!

427
00:27:17,940 --> 00:27:18,600
Let's go!

428
00:27:19,180 --> 00:27:19,620
Alright!

429
00:27:26,440 --> 00:27:27,720
Kankichi, can you hear me?

430
00:27:27,960 --> 00:27:28,780
Yeah, I can.

431
00:27:29,640 --> 00:27:32,260
The seafood squad is
heading for Ryogoku Bridge.

432
00:27:32,260 --> 00:27:34,200
Got it!

433
00:27:37,320 --> 00:27:40,200
Hey, Suna!

434
00:27:40,620 --> 00:27:40,980
Right!

435
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:43,780
Damn it, it's empty!

436
00:27:44,320 --> 00:27:45,660
Boss Ryotsu, over there!

437
00:27:45,820 --> 00:27:48,680
Yeah, are they planning
to escape into Tokyo Bay?

438
00:27:49,240 --> 00:27:52,040
Don't think you can get away from me!

439
00:27:54,220 --> 00:27:55,560
Ten drones, right?

440
00:27:55,560 --> 00:27:56,520
Understood.

441
00:27:59,900 --> 00:28:02,660
If we get this far,
they can't follow us anymore.

442
00:28:03,240 --> 00:28:05,600
Kankichi will definitely come to help us.

443
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:07,700
I believe in you, Kankichi.

444
00:28:12,180 --> 00:28:13,180
What is that?

445
00:28:22,620 --> 00:28:25,000
Mischievous and playful,
aren't you bewildered?

446
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:28,340
Loving the sea, protecting justice!

447
00:28:28,340 --> 00:28:30,220
Who called? Poseidon!

448
00:28:30,220 --> 00:28:32,900
I'll put you in the chest of drawers,
Tansu-Nigon!

449
00:28:33,760 --> 00:28:37,560
A black detective?
One of the Sunbaga Glass? Dolphin, is it?

450
00:28:38,340 --> 00:28:39,780
Harowima Kendan!

451
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:46,360
We've come to take it back.

452
00:28:49,340 --> 00:28:50,800
Well then, I'm off.

453
00:28:53,260 --> 00:28:55,740
Senpai, please be careful.

454
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:05,700
We'll blast our guns and
break through by force!

455
00:29:08,660 --> 00:29:10,240
Come on, Dolphin!

456
00:29:22,980 --> 00:29:23,440
Amazing!

457
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:27,220
They're eating it up!
If this works, they'll go wild for more!

458
00:29:38,280 --> 00:29:39,600
Yes, yes, that's it!

459
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:41,820
I'll show you an even more amazing trick!

460
00:29:50,660 --> 00:29:51,880
Bravo!

461
00:29:54,280 --> 00:29:55,880
Did you see that divine feat?

462
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:01,500
W-where did they go?

463
00:30:05,160 --> 00:30:06,840
Damn it!

464
00:30:09,560 --> 00:30:10,500
*Slump*

465
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:12,300
Damn it, what the hell are you doing?!

466
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:13,320
Kanbichi!

467
00:30:13,320 --> 00:30:14,800
What's wrong?

468
00:30:15,960 --> 00:30:20,860
Ahead of the kidnappers, a large
cruiser of unknown nationality is moored.

469
00:30:21,240 --> 00:30:23,200
They plan to board it.

470
00:30:23,200 --> 00:30:26,860
If they escape to the Pacific on that cruiser,
we're in serious trouble.

471
00:30:26,860 --> 00:30:28,820
We have to do something before then.

472
00:30:31,840 --> 00:30:33,000
Nooooo!

473
00:30:34,100 --> 00:30:36,180
Colonel Bergryu came after all!

474
00:30:36,580 --> 00:30:41,000
The kidnappers are going to switch to
that large cruiser ahead and escape!

475
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:44,760
I see, so we just need
to sink it before then.

476
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:46,920
Leave it to me.

477
00:30:49,340 --> 00:30:50,760
It's about time.

478
00:30:50,760 --> 00:30:52,200
This'll be a walk in the park.

479
00:30:57,460 --> 00:30:59,000
N-no way...

480
00:31:00,100 --> 00:31:01,000
Rock'n

481
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:02,540
Flyer

482
00:31:03,300 --> 00:31:04,020
I'm serious.

483
00:31:07,660 --> 00:31:08,780
W-what is it?

484
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:20,220
Brazil!

485
00:31:22,080 --> 00:31:23,280
They made a U-turn!

486
00:31:23,500 --> 00:31:26,200
Ryotsu, should we sink the motorboat too?

487
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:28,220
That bastard's fast! Lemon's on board!

488
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:30,540
Ha that's right!

489
00:31:30,720 --> 00:31:31,920
I'll call for backup!

490
00:31:32,180 --> 00:31:35,020
I'm praying for your success! Good luck!

491
00:31:44,600 --> 00:31:45,260
Lead!

492
00:31:45,260 --> 00:31:46,240
What's wrong?

493
00:31:46,500 --> 00:31:48,960
Looks like some weird guy is tailing us.

494
00:31:50,360 --> 00:31:52,500
That attack chopper is his doing too

495
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:54,580
I'll shoot it down.

496
00:31:56,120 --> 00:31:56,920
I'll shoot you down!

497
00:31:56,920 --> 00:31:57,400
Stop it!

498
00:31:57,400 --> 00:32:00,360
We don't have any weapons, you know!

499
00:32:00,360 --> 00:32:01,100
We don't have any weapons, you know!

500
00:32:01,100 --> 00:32:01,980
Over there!

501
00:32:02,440 --> 00:32:02,840
Yes.

502
00:32:04,140 --> 00:32:06,200
Take this, you crew-cut bastard!

503
00:32:07,420 --> 00:32:08,800
This way this time?

504
00:32:08,800 --> 00:32:10,220
This way this time?

505
00:32:10,220 --> 00:32:13,520
This one's beeping!

506
00:32:15,900 --> 00:32:16,780
What is it?

507
00:32:20,420 --> 00:32:21,300
What's wrong?

508
00:32:21,660 --> 00:32:23,340
A weird guy

509
00:32:26,060 --> 00:32:27,880
It's not just the bulge in his crotch.

510
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:29,980
When an incident happens on land,

511
00:32:29,980 --> 00:32:32,420
he solves everything
in just his swim trunks.

512
00:32:33,520 --> 00:32:36,240
One of the Special Criminal
Investigation Division's Samba Glass.

513
00:32:36,800 --> 00:32:38,040
In swim trunks

514
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:40,140
Just arrived!

515
00:32:40,140 --> 00:32:41,180
Boo! Boo!

516
00:32:41,180 --> 00:32:47,080
Haa, he really does sound like a pervert, doesn't he?
Kamaa's... Krisuku name.

517
00:32:47,500 --> 00:32:48,260
Roger!

518
00:32:51,040 --> 00:32:52,320
Aaaaaah!

519
00:32:55,660 --> 00:32:59,700
That swim trunks guy, what's he going to pull out today?
The classic banana...

520
00:32:59,700 --> 00:33:03,320
Which prefecture...

521
00:33:04,820 --> 00:33:06,060
Whoa, amazing!

522
00:33:11,060 --> 00:33:13,520
You let the enemy get away,
and you still want to look cool?

523
00:33:14,420 --> 00:33:15,360
Don't get cocky, Ryotsu.

524
00:33:15,780 --> 00:33:19,600
I fired a GPS transmitter
instead of a bullet.

525
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:22,440
Wow, you've really won me over,
swim trunks and all.

526
00:33:25,760 --> 00:33:26,760
How embarrassing.

527
00:33:27,920 --> 00:33:28,700
Ryotsu.

528
00:33:29,260 --> 00:33:31,660
The kidnappers told us the handover location

529
00:33:31,660 --> 00:33:33,540
for the 10 billion yen ransom.

530
00:33:34,620 --> 00:33:35,560
Haneda Airport.

531
00:33:36,240 --> 00:33:38,620
They also demanded that we
provide a chartered plane,

532
00:33:40,140 --> 00:33:48,420
so with the GPS transmitter on, we can track the kidnappers' location now.
Guide us there

533
00:33:48,420 --> 00:33:48,740
please.

534
00:33:54,380 --> 00:33:55,720
Get on the expressway!

535
00:34:01,140 --> 00:34:03,200
Fine, turn right there!

536
00:34:04,200 --> 00:34:14,200


537
00:34:14,200 --> 00:34:17,320
It's not just a transformation,
bathed in the moon's energy on my back!

538
00:34:17,320 --> 00:34:18,900
Turn there!

539
00:34:19,140 --> 00:34:21,740
Yes! If it's an aerial incident...

540
00:34:22,720 --> 00:34:25,560
Hey! Come on!
The factory isn't finished yet!

541
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:33,720
Not yet!

542
00:34:34,260 --> 00:34:34,980
Turn!

543
00:34:40,840 --> 00:34:41,480
Chief!

544
00:34:41,760 --> 00:34:44,940
We're driving the kidnappers
toward the Tokyo Skytree.

545
00:34:44,940 --> 00:34:46,980
Send the backup units.

546
00:34:46,980 --> 00:34:49,680
And have them fire on
the Skytree's visitors.

547
00:34:50,160 --> 00:34:50,880
Understood.

548
00:34:53,620 --> 00:34:54,660
No way!

549
00:35:04,980 --> 00:35:20,100


550
00:35:48,520 --> 00:35:53,080
Thank you for watching.

551
00:35:55,680 --> 00:36:23,000
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa!

552
00:36:43,520 --> 00:36:44,860
You can't run anymore!

553
00:36:44,860 --> 00:36:47,100
Drop your weapons and raise your hands!

554
00:36:47,540 --> 00:36:48,260
Die.

555
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:53,520
Looks like it's game over for you.

556
00:36:54,300 --> 00:36:55,400
We'll see about that.

557
00:37:03,740 --> 00:37:05,640
They've even got bombs ready.

558
00:37:06,140 --> 00:37:07,880
Come any closer and see what happens.

559
00:37:07,880 --> 00:37:10,000
The princess and her friends don't appear.

560
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:11,400
As expected of the leader.

561
00:37:12,820 --> 00:37:13,420
Stop it!

562
00:37:13,780 --> 00:37:14,860
Let that girl go!

563
00:37:15,360 --> 00:37:17,260
I'm the real Sabrina!

564
00:37:17,420 --> 00:37:17,880
What!?

565
00:37:18,380 --> 00:37:19,440
What are you talking about!

566
00:37:19,500 --> 00:37:20,600
The real one is over here!

567
00:37:21,700 --> 00:37:23,720
But I can't let you be put in
danger any longer.

568
00:37:23,720 --> 00:37:24,940
I can't let you face this danger.

569
00:37:25,420 --> 00:37:26,080
Yah!

570
00:37:26,260 --> 00:37:27,320
Whether she's a princess,

571
00:37:27,340 --> 00:37:28,100
or a fake,

572
00:37:28,140 --> 00:37:28,600
it doesn't matter!

573
00:37:29,020 --> 00:37:30,800
If this bomb goes off,

574
00:37:30,960 --> 00:37:32,500
everything within a 500-meter radius

575
00:37:32,540 --> 00:37:33,840
will become a sea of fire!

576
00:37:34,380 --> 00:37:35,000
Now,

577
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:36,740
leave one patrol car behind,

578
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:38,920
and everyone clear out of here!

579
00:37:41,460 --> 00:37:42,960
Aaaaaaah!

580
00:37:45,820 --> 00:37:46,940
Aaaaaaah!

581
00:37:51,420 --> 00:37:53,660
Too bad, it's too late now.

582
00:37:53,660 --> 00:37:54,920
Aaaaaaah!

583
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:03,020
Granny, is Lemon okay again?

584
00:38:03,020 --> 00:38:05,520
Thank goodness, Lemon-chan!

585
00:38:05,520 --> 00:38:06,640
Sabrina!

586
00:38:42,760 --> 00:38:43,180
Go ahead!

587
00:38:55,980 --> 00:38:57,660
Ya, ya, ya!

588
00:38:57,660 --> 00:39:00,680
Senpai?

589
00:39:03,480 --> 00:39:04,200
Senpai?

590
00:39:04,600 --> 00:39:06,340
Kankichi, where do you think you're going?

591
00:39:10,760 --> 00:39:12,660
If we use the elevator,
we'll never make it in time!

592
00:39:12,780 --> 00:39:14,660
Nurarararara!

593
00:39:17,820 --> 00:39:18,940
Yahoo!

594
00:39:18,940 --> 00:39:35,740
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

595
00:39:35,740 --> 00:39:37,840
So he went up to the top of the Skytree?

596
00:39:38,660 --> 00:39:40,100
So that's what it was.

597
00:39:40,480 --> 00:39:43,640
Trying to minimize the
damage from the explosion

598
00:39:44,640 --> 00:39:46,920
Kankichi, you really are something.

599
00:39:47,920 --> 00:39:51,420
Do your best, Kankichi.
We're counting on you.

600
00:39:52,700 --> 00:40:01,800
Alright, we're running out of time!

601
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:03,340
Gaaah!

602
00:40:03,340 --> 00:40:04,140
Gaaah!

603
00:40:04,160 --> 00:40:04,900
Gaaah!

604
00:40:06,340 --> 00:40:07,920
Gaaah!

605
00:40:09,460 --> 00:40:10,600
Let's do our best with this!

606
00:40:10,980 --> 00:40:11,460
Gaaah!

607
00:40:12,360 --> 00:40:14,700
If it comes to this,
we've got no choice but to climb up!

608
00:40:15,320 --> 00:40:15,940
Gaaah!

609
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:16,580
Gaaah!

610
00:40:16,580 --> 00:40:16,960
Gaaah!

611
00:40:16,960 --> 00:40:17,280
Gaaah!

612
00:40:24,440 --> 00:40:26,760
All that's left is to throw it far away!

613
00:40:27,600 --> 00:40:28,040
All that's left is to throw it far away!

614
00:41:25,820 --> 00:41:26,720
Kankichi

615
00:41:26,720 --> 00:41:30,140
Kankichi can't possibly be dead.

616
00:41:46,820 --> 00:41:48,520
Gakiji

617
00:42:12,200 --> 00:42:19,180
!

618
00:42:19,840 --> 00:42:20,980
Where am I?

619
00:42:22,540 --> 00:42:24,440
If it isn't King Yama!

620
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:25,860
Long time no see.

621
00:42:26,860 --> 00:42:28,760
Didn't expect you to show up again.

622
00:42:28,760 --> 00:42:31,380
So that means I've died

623
00:42:31,900 --> 00:42:32,260
That's right.

624
00:42:33,240 --> 00:42:34,180
Guess it can't be helped.

625
00:42:34,640 --> 00:42:36,260
Just pass your judgment already.

626
00:42:37,140 --> 00:42:38,840
Bring me the Judgment Mirror.

627
00:42:43,680 --> 00:42:46,960
I protected the Shitamachi
and saved many people's lives.

628
00:42:46,960 --> 00:42:48,560
Obviously I'm going to heaven, right?

629
00:42:49,180 --> 00:42:55,200
Look at how many wicked deeds the people of this town have done!
They're all headed for hell!

630
00:42:55,200 --> 00:43:02,080
Don't lump me in with them! Look at all those people who crowded in front of me,
the ones who didn't want to go to hell!

631
00:43:02,600 --> 00:43:04,620
So that means I'm going to the Tengu realm

632
00:43:04,620 --> 00:43:10,960
Apparently they won't even let me into heaven.
What's that supposed to mean?

633
00:43:11,620 --> 00:43:14,060
Then where am I supposed to go?

634
00:43:17,560 --> 00:43:18,980
It can't be helped.

635
00:43:44,060 --> 00:43:59,580
Uuuuuuuugh...

636
00:43:59,580 --> 00:44:29,540
Eeeeeeeeh... Yeah, yeah, yeah...

637
00:44:29,580 --> 00:44:31,580
Even at a conservative estimate,
that'd cost at least 100 million yen.

638
00:44:32,600 --> 00:44:33,720
Good morning.

639
00:44:33,720 --> 00:44:34,840
Morning.

640
00:44:35,300 --> 00:44:37,700
Didn't die even in that massive explosion

641
00:44:38,200 --> 00:44:39,840
Are you hurt anywhere?

642
00:44:39,840 --> 00:44:41,920
I'm totally fine.

643
00:44:41,920 --> 00:44:44,740
I might even be healthier than before.

644
00:44:45,520 --> 00:44:48,340
Feels like I've been reborn

645
00:44:49,060 --> 00:44:51,820
Ryotsu's like a cockroach, I guess.

646
00:44:51,820 --> 00:44:52,480
Any complaints?

647
00:44:52,480 --> 00:44:55,480
Don't you think that's a bit harsh
for a hero who saved the old town?

648
00:44:56,380 --> 00:44:59,420
If you say things like that,
you'll set social media on fire.

649
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:03,000
It's not like I'd set anything
on fire if I hadn't done it.

650
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:04,180
Give me a break.

651
00:45:04,740 --> 00:45:07,240
Praising me a little wouldn't hurt,
you know.

652
00:45:07,740 --> 00:45:08,380
Yeah, you're right.

653
00:45:08,380 --> 00:45:10,740
Well done, Ryotsu.

654
00:45:10,740 --> 00:45:11,440
Right, right.

655
00:45:12,240 --> 00:45:13,500
I almost forgot.

656
00:45:13,500 --> 00:45:16,520
A bill came from the Skytree.

657
00:45:18,300 --> 00:45:19,460
10 billion yen.

658
00:45:20,440 --> 00:45:21,520
What are you going to do, Ryotsu?

659
00:45:21,520 --> 00:45:22,700
Will you pay in cash?

660
00:45:22,700 --> 00:45:25,280
Or will you pay it off over 30 years?

661
00:45:25,760 --> 00:45:27,200
I'm not accepting that.

662
00:45:27,200 --> 00:45:29,580
Hey, hey, Ryotsu, wait!

663
00:45:29,940 --> 00:45:32,380
Even if we sold it all off at once,
we couldn't pay it.

664
00:45:32,380 --> 00:45:34,280
Hey, stop right there, Ryotsu!

665
00:45:34,280 --> 00:45:38,800
I absolutely will not accept it.

666
00:45:55,480 --> 00:46:00,740
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling.

667
00:46:01,940 --> 00:46:07,400
Walking while looking back,
pulled along by the clatter.

668
00:46:08,460 --> 00:46:14,620
That strange feeling I had back then.

669
00:46:15,360 --> 00:46:19,800
So, on the arcade's tiles,

670
00:46:19,800 --> 00:46:25,600
I tried walking only on the black ones.

671
00:46:28,080 --> 00:46:33,880
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

672
00:46:34,800 --> 00:46:41,220
Even the self-important politicians
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow.

673
00:46:41,680 --> 00:46:46,860
Come on, turn that corner.

674
00:46:47,800 --> 00:46:51,980
You'll get to see everyone, everyone.

675
00:46:52,540 --> 00:46:56,640
Over there, Kameari.

676
00:46:57,440 --> 00:46:59,940
Surely, Kameari is there.

677
00:47:01,180 --> 00:47:05,120
Everyone, come on over to our town!

678
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:06,720
Thank you.

679
00:47:09,680 --> 00:47:13,820
After this,
there's a message from Akimoto-sensei.

680
00:47:20,080 --> 00:47:23,140
Did everyone enjoy it?

681
00:47:23,920 --> 00:47:25,640
Thanks for everything until now.

682
00:47:26,820 --> 00:47:27,740
See you.

